      "message": "OK.  So I would propose that passing through \"mysql_storage_engine\" plainly like this is too fine grained.  It implies that someone could stick \"MyISAM\" or \"ARIA\" in there, which is not the case; things will break badly.  In oslo.db, the fact that one wants to use \"ndb\" should be a coarse-grained configuration setting; \"CONF.database.mysql_use_ndb\"; then here, mysql_engine would call upon an oslo_db function called \"get_effective_mysql_engine(conn)\" - it\u0027s passed a Connection or Engine (migrate_engine here is an Engine).  Connection/Engine.info will have the \"use_ndb\" flag inside of it which was set up within oslo.db.engines.create_engine().   This allows the consumption of CONF.database.* to remain local to the Engine object that gets set up without a separate need to track CONF.* settings to it; then oslo.db is called upon to make the determination what it means to be \"ndb\" or \"non ndb\".",
